Z||000000||ITB 2M4||11-13-2001||12:53 PM||||Finally, a place for Fiero enthusiasts that hasn't gone belly up, and is actually going quite strong!<P>I own 4 Fiero's all together.  Two '84's, one of which I race in the Sports Car Club of America's Improved Touring B class, the other is pretty much a parts car now.  An '85 which is also a parts car, and an '87 which will probably see the street again, if I don't put a roll cage in it as well.  It's got a few dings, but it's in so much better shape than the '84 was when I turned it into a race car.  I basically tore the '84 all the way down to the skeleton, and put it all back together by myself.  I even built the motor (my first motor) that's in it now.  Unfortunatly, it only makes 88hp at the rear wheels, which is about 20hp to low for my class.  Hopefully I can get some good info on the 2.5L here.<BR>I'm running the Koni suspension package from the Fiero Store, but the car still sits about 1 1/2 inches to high.  It's got an Accusump 3qt reservoir, oil cooler and a remote filter, for a total of 10 qts of oil, so it shouldn't have any oil problems.  I'm running the K&N filter, and Headman headers with straight exhaust.  You can't really do to much to the engine except balance and blueprint, plus port match the head to the gaskets an inch into the head.  If anyone is a 2.5 expert, I could really use the help.  Hope to hear from my fellow Fiero friends!<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4||||reg||1
